# The release-lock vectors this repository's reader is checked against.
#
# The vectors live in mica and are READ AT THIS COMMIT, not copied: a copy is a
# snapshot, and on 2026-09-20 five repositories each held a different one. The
# basename is uniform across the workspace (coordinator ruling) so that finding
# every reader's pin is one command rather than a maintained list of paths.
#
# NOT locks/pins/: that directory means "a producer release we consume", mica
# publishes no releases, and forcing it there would mean relaxing mica-pin v1 to
# make RELEASE optional -- weakening a validated format for a thing it was not
# designed for. Not a git row in locks/upstream.lock either: that file is for
# third-party inputs, and a row there would assert mica is upstream of us.
#
# KNOWN DEFECTS AT THIS COMMIT: none. The x64-to-uefi-x64 sweep of 2026-09-16
# renamed a third-party download URL in ten vector files
# (bun-linux-x64.zip became bun-linux-uefi-x64.zip, while the arm64 row beside
# it was untouched because "aarch64" contains no "x64"); mica repaired it in
# ddf4edc8 and this commit is later. A pin is a statement about ONE commit and
# never about the newest one, so this gate will not notice a later fix or a
# later defect on its own -- when mica moves, this line moves with it.
REPOSITORY=mica
COMMIT=b2e3044ebfdef6df7e8e939e451c14eff3fc2e72
